  "Save selected photos": "保存所選照片",
  "Connecting to upload space...": "正在連接上傳空間…",
  "Upload instructor audio and video/record Tang Qiuming’s voice": "上傳導師音視頻 / 錄製唐秋鳴的聲音",
  "The photo is saved for facial reconstruction and does not automatically replace the current digital person.": "照片保存後用於面部重建，不會自動替換目前的數字人。",
  "Upload workspace": "上傳空間",
  "After entering the password, you can upload photos, audio and video, and recordings.": "輸入密碼後，可上傳照片、音視頻和錄音。",
  "Password": "密碼",
  "enter": "進入",
  "Tang Qiuming’s guide voice": "唐秋鳴的導覽聲音",
  "Tang Qiuming / Soochow University": "唐秋鳴 / 蘇州大學",
  "Record your voice for the tour": "給導覽留下你的聲音",
  "As if you were introducing the project to a professor,": "像向老師介紹項目一樣，",
  "take your time.": "慢慢說就好。",
  "Four short paragraphs, each about half a minute. Read at your usual speaking speed, without deliberately using a broadcasting tone. If you make a mistake in reading it, you can re-record it, listen to it first and then save it if you are satisfied.": "四段短文，每段約半分鐘。按你平時的語速讀，不必刻意用播音腔。讀錯了可以重錄，先試聽滿意再保存。",
  "Upload the instructor’s audio and video and prepare the preface →": "上傳導師音視頻，準備前言 →",
  "Upload a photo of the instructor’s face →": "上傳導師面部照片 →",
  "Preparing for a reading": "正在準備朗讀稿",
  "Start when you're ready": "準備好後開始",
  "Start recording": "開始錄音",
  "end recording": "結束錄音",
  "Save this recording": "保存這一段",
  "Download backup": "下載備份",
  "Connecting to recording space...": "正在連接錄音空間…",
  "next paragraph": "下一段",
  "before recording": "錄之前",
  "Find a quiet room with your phone or microphone about a palm's length away from your mouth. Don't play music, and don't turn on noise reduction or reverb.": "找一個安靜的房間，手機或麥克風離嘴約一掌。不要播放音樂，也別開降噪美聲或混響。",
  "The first paragraph is a natural introduction, the second paragraph explains the operation, the third paragraph is full of questions, and the fourth paragraph is like inviting the other party to give it a try. Keep your own pauses and don't imitate someone else's voice.": "第一段自然介紹，第二段解釋操作，第三段帶着疑問，第四段像邀請對方試一試。保留你自己的停頓，不用模仿別人的聲音。",
  "How to use it in the future": "以後怎樣使用",
  "These recordings serve as your tone reference. The guides of different instructors still use their own text, and then the corresponding explanations are generated by the timbre model and saved on the server for reuse.": "這些錄音作爲你的音色參考。不同導師的導覽仍然使用各自的文字，之後由音色模型生成對應講解，並在服務端保存複用。",
  "After saving the recording, you still need to perform sound generation and audition verification; currently, the navigation sound will not be directly replaced. The recording will not be put into the public music library.": "保存錄音後，還需要進行音色生成和試聽驗證；當前不會直接替換導覽聲音。錄音不放進公開曲庫。",
  "saved": "已保存",
  "Not connected yet": "尚未連接",
  "My recordings are kept separately from authorized instructor materials. This page will not submit recordings to third-party voice platforms.": "本人錄音與獲授權的導師素材分開保存。本頁不會把錄音提交給第三方語音平臺。",
  "Tang Qiuming | Research and Demo": "唐秋鳴｜研究與演示",
  "Enter the workspace ↗": "進入工作區 ↗",
  "2027 PhD Application·Project Guide": "2027 博士申請 · 項目導覽",
  "play together,": "一起演奏，",
  "What does it mean to truly play together?": "怎樣纔算真正合在一起？",
  "I started with an off-site MIDI ensemble. After putting the notes on the same timeline, I want to ask: Is it the network delay that we are correcting, or the bit of breath that the performer originally wanted to keep?": "我從異地 MIDI 合奏做起。把音符放到同一條時間線上之後，我想追問：我們校正的究竟是網絡延遲，還是演奏者本來想保留的那一點呼吸？",
  "Soochow University Conservatory of Music Music Education Major Piano Direction": "蘇州大學音樂學院　音樂教育專業鋼琴方向",
  "Class of 2024 Master’s Degree Students": "2024 級碩士研究生",
  "Choose what you would like to explore": "選擇本次交流的切入點",
  "Professor’s name (optional)": "導師姓名（可不填）",
  "Ensemble playing and human–computer collaboration": "合奏與人機協作",
  "Music generation and evaluation": "音樂生成與評價",
  "Start the project tour": "開始項目導覽",
  "Create a personalised demo link": "生成專屬演示鏈接",
  "About 4 minutes. You can switch back and forth at any time, or enter the real workspace for operation.": "約 4 分鐘。可隨時前後切換，也可以進入真實工作區操作。",
  "View in workspace ↗": "在工作區查看 ↗",
  "Next →": "下一步 →",
  "01 / Already have a job": "01 / 已有工作",
  "Timecode-based offsite MIDI ensemble": "基於時間碼的異地 MIDI 合奏",
  "Connect remote performances with timecode synchronization, delay compensation and local source rendering. This is the main project of the application; the specific experimental conditions, delay measurement and number of participants will be added after the original records are compiled.": "以時間碼同步、延遲補償和本地音源渲染連接異地演奏。這是申請的主要項目；具體實驗條件、延遲測量和參與人數將在整理原始記錄後補充。",
  "02 / Current prototype": "02 / 當前原型",
  "Bringing sheet music, performance and practice sessions together": "把樂譜、演奏和練習過程放到一起",
  "The current webpage provides music score import, electronic score, playback, follow-up and background tasks. It is an engineering prototype used to explore problems. There are still errors in music recognition and automatic orchestration that need to be verified.": "當前網頁提供琴譜導入、電子譜、播放、跟彈和後臺任務。它是用於探索問題的工程原型，識譜與自動配器仍有需要驗證的誤差。",
  "03/Proposed research questions": "03 / 擬研究問題",
  "Where should synchronisation stop?": "同步的邊界在哪裏？",
  "Given measurable network jitter, how does a system differentiate between transmission delays and intentional cadence processing? Would different compensation strategies change the way the ensemble listens and adjusts to each other?": "在可測量的網絡抖動下，系統怎樣區分傳輸延遲與有意的節奏處理？不同的補償策略，會不會改變合奏者彼此傾聽和調整的方式？",
  "Tang Qiuming · 20245248013@stu.suda.edu.cn": "唐秋鳴 · 20245248013@stu.suda.edu.cn",
  "Research ideas and implemented functions are presented separately": "研究設想與已實現功能分開展示",
  "More scores": "更多曲譜",
  "Refresh scores": "重新整理曲譜",
  "Why I started with ensemble playing": "先說說我爲什麼做這個",
  "I play piano and accompany other musicians. I began exploring remote MIDI ensembles because I wanted people in different places to rehearse together. This website is a later piano-learning prototype, separate from the remote ensemble system. I would like to use it to show you a few questions I am still working through. Please pause and explore whenever you like.": "我在蘇州大學讀音樂教育，主項是鋼琴，也做伴奏。碩士期間，我做過基於時間碼的異地 MIDI 合奏，想讓不在同一間琴房的人也能一起排練。做着做着，我開始在意一個問題：時間對上了，兩個人聽起來就一定合得好嗎？我還想知道，他們各自是怎麼聽、怎麼等對方的。您現在看到的是後來做的鋼琴教學網頁，我想用一首具體的曲子，給您看看它能做什麼，也說說我遇到的問題。",
  "Choose a piece in the full-screen library": "您挑一首熟悉的曲子",
  "Please choose a piece you know. A familiar melody makes it easier to hear when something is wrong. We will follow the same piece through the demonstration.\n\nSearch for a title above and select a card. I will wait for the score to load before continuing. You can also skip this step for an overview.": "先請您挑一首熟悉的曲子。我會把曲庫展開，您可以搜歌名，也可以直接點封面。熟悉的作品，哪一處聽着彆扭，通常很快就能聽出來。我們就用這一首往下看。點開後等譜子載入，我再接着講；想先看整體的話，也可以跳過選曲。",
  "Start with the score you have": "譜子從這裏放進來",
  "Scores come in different forms: PDFs, photographs of printed pages, or sometimes just a recording. These import options let you start with what you already have. Photographs can be put in page order before processing.\n\nUploading a file is not the same as obtaining a usable score. I have encountered merged left- and right-hand parts and misread time signatures. The original is retained so that the electronic score can be checked. This matters especially in teaching research: otherwise we may mistake software errors for evidence about a student.": "這裏可以導入 PDF、曲譜照片、MIDI、MusicXML，也可以放音視頻。照片要先把幾頁按順序傳齊，再開始識別。拿到什麼材料，就從相應的入口放進來。\n\n識別以後，我還是要回頭看原稿。這個項目以前出過左右手混在一起、四四拍讀成四二拍的問題，後面播放就跟着錯了。所以我把原稿留在旁邊，方便檢查拍號、音符和時值。用於教學之前，這些地方得先覈對。",
  "Listen to a short passage": "先聽一小段",
  "Choose a familiar passage, play it, then slow it down and follow the score. One recurring problem took me a long time to resolve: the notes appeared correct, but playback paused at the end of measures. Investigating meter and duration parsing showed why changing the piano sound alone could not help.\n\nThat experience made me more careful about expressive playback. Music needs room to breathe, but the beat must remain reliable. I want to establish accurate rhythm before shaping dynamics, phrase endings and the balance between the hands. Listen to whether the accompaniment supports the melody.": "您可以先播放一段，再把速度放慢，對着譜聽。我之前反覆遇到一個毛病：明明譜上沒寫休止，到了小節末尾卻停了一下。往回查，才發現拍號、時值和播放時間的處理都會影響它。這類問題還得用不同的譜子逐一檢查。\n\n我很在意左手的伴奏。音都彈對了，聽着也可能很硬；但爲了讓它自然一點，又不能把節奏弄得忽快忽慢。您聽這一段時，可以留意左手和旋律的關係，尤其是句尾怎麼接過去。",
  "What does a student do after seeing feedback?": "這一遍練完，學生學會了嗎",
  "This is the question I most want to investigate. A system can highlight wrong notes and timing errors, but has the student understood them, or simply followed the prompts once more? The next score alone cannot tell us.\n\nI would begin with a small comparison: the same passage and the same practice time, with one group receiving live prompts and another receiving feedback after each phrase. Then both play without prompts. Alongside errors, I would observe where they stop and restart. This is a proposed experiment, not a conclusion already reached. You can expand the practice controls here; microphone access must be enabled explicitly.": "跟彈需要在這裏開啓麥克風。演奏時，程序會對照譜子給出錯音和節奏提示。這個功能做出來以後，我更想知道學生怎麼用它：他會停下來聽那一處，還是看着提示又從頭彈一遍？分數高了一點，暫時還回答不了這個問題。\n\n我準備比較演奏中提示和樂句結束後提示，兩邊練習時間一樣，再關掉提示請學生彈一次。除了錯音，我也想記錄他在哪裏停、從哪裏重來。這還是一個待做的實驗，您可以先展開看看操作。",
  "Do these parts work together?": "聽聽這幾個聲部",
  "Here you can choose an ensemble and inspect the generated instrumental parts. My least satisfactory results are arrangements whose individual lines seem plausible but compete when combined. Checking instrumental ranges alone is clearly not enough.\n\nI want to pay closer attention to what happens after generation: how parts enter, how they leave space for the melody, and whether a student can actually play them. For teaching, I would rather develop a few dependable textures than offer many polished-looking arrangements that are difficult to use.": "這裏可以選編制，查看和試聽各個聲部。最讓我卡住的是，有些生成結果單獨聽還能接受，合起來卻很吵。絃樂一直填滿，鼓也跟着每個鋼琴音敲，主旋律就被蓋住了。音域沒有越界，和聲與聲部的關係也未必成立。\n\n我希望先把幾種常用的織體做好，檢查哪些地方該進入、哪些地方該留空，再考慮學生能不能彈。您可以單獨聽一個聲部，然後合起來聽。生成的結果還需要覈對和試奏，我不想把它直接當成已經合適的教學材料。",
  "Keep waiting in the background": "識譜進度在這裏",
  "This page looks technical, but it affects whether someone can use the system comfortably. Recognition and arranging take time. Blocking the page interrupts the musical idea a person was following. The queue allows users to inspect the original or listen to completed material while processing continues.\n\nThese are real tasks. You can see the piece and processing stage. When something fails, the system should explain where it stopped. Handling delays and errors is part of designing a tool for learning.": "識譜和改編比較費時間，所以我把它們放在後臺。等待時，您仍然可以看原稿、聽已經載入的作品。任務中心會列出正在處理哪首曲子、做到哪一步，也可以調整先處理哪一項。\n\n這個地方我也改過很多次。以前有任務一直顯示等待，卻看不出在等誰；還有的失敗以後只報一個代碼。我希望現在能把原因說清楚，讓使用者知道接下來是繼續等、重試，還是換一份材料。",
  "A question I would like to discuss": "我接下來想弄清楚的事",
  "I would like to return to remote MIDI duets, control network latency and compare compensation methods. Beyond measuring the time between two notes, I want to know whether performers are continually chasing one another or can still lead a musical phrase. I would value your thoughts on that distinction.": "回到我最早做的異地 MIDI 合奏，接下來我想先把範圍縮到兩個人，比較幾種延遲補償辦法。同樣一段音樂，補償以後，他們會不會一直在追對方？想帶起一個樂句的時候，另一個人還能不能接住？時間誤差可以測，但這幾件事怎麼記錄、怎麼比較，我還需要認真設計。您覺得從哪一種演奏任務開始，比較容易看清這個問題？",
  "I study music education. While building this website, I kept coming back to one question: after we point out a wrong note, how does a student practise the passage next time? I would like to show you the prototype first, then discuss which forms of feedback are worth investigating in the classroom.": "我是音樂教育專業的學生，平時彈鋼琴，也帶過鋼琴學生。做這個網頁，我最想弄清楚的是：學生看見一個錯音提示，下一遍會怎樣練？再彈對一次，可能是聽明白了，也可能只是記住提示。我想先請您看看現在的操作，再聊聊這個問題該怎樣放進教學實驗裏。",
  "I would start by comparing live feedback with feedback given after a phrase. With practice time held constant, can students still correct the passage when the prompts are removed? I think that matters more than an immediate improvement in their score. The experiment still needs careful design.": "我想先做一個小一點的比較：練同一段、用相同的時間，一種在演奏中提示，另一種等樂句結束再提示。然後把提示關掉，請學生再彈。這樣才能看看，他離開這個網頁以後還會不會處理那一處。哪些練習動作值得記錄，多久以後再測一次比較合適，我還拿不準，想聽聽您的意見。",
  "Generating a score that can be played is one thing; making its parts work together is much harder. This prototype keeps generation, listening and checking in one place. I would like to show you what works so far and where I am still getting stuck.": "我在蘇州大學讀音樂教育，主項是鋼琴。這個網頁裏的編配，我改了不少次，仍有些地方不滿意。鋼琴、絃樂和鼓的音符都生成出來了，可一起放的時候，有時很吵，旋律反而聽不清。我要把它拿來做練習材料，就還得檢查和聲、聲部和難度。我們挑一首曲子，邊聽邊看，這樣比我只介紹用了什麼模型更清楚。",
  "I would narrow the question to graded practice materials. If we preserve the structure of a piece and constrain its parts and difficulty, do the generated exercises become more useful for teaching? I would involve teachers through blind assessment and students through actual playing, rather than rely on the generating model to judge its own output.": "如果繼續做下去，我想先限定一種教學用途，比如給不同程度的學生準備同一首作品的練習版本。保持原曲結構，逐步改變聲部和難度，再請老師看譜、讓學生試奏。我想知道哪些限制真的能讓材料更好用。要評到什麼程度，才足以說這一版適合某個學習階段？這個問題我想再往下做。"
}